# What the container engine may not send to the daemon when building
# serving/Dockerfile from the repository root.
#
# The build context is the whole repository, but the serving image needs
# startlingly little of it: two Python modules, one requirements manifest, and
# the exported model. Everything else is excluded, which keeps the context small
# and - more to the point - keeps a local .venv, a tracking store or a stray
# credential file from ever being copied into a layer by accident.
#
# Note what is *not* here: serving/model/. That directory is the model the image
# serves, and excluding it would produce an image that builds and then fails to
# start.

# Version control and repository metadata.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.gitattributes

# Local environments and caches. A virtual environment built on the host would
# be both enormous and wrong for the image's architecture.
.venv
venv
env
ENV
.env
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
*.egg-info
build
dist

# The local MLflow tracking store. The model reaches the image as an exported
# directory, never as a whole run history.
mlruns
mlartifacts

# Everything the serving image has no use for. Note that automobile/ is *not*
# excluded: the pickled model refers to a function in it by name, so the module
# has to be importable inside the image for the artifact to unpickle at all.
tests
notebooks
data
docs
charts
.pipelines
.claude
.flake8
pyproject.toml
README.md
CLAUDE.md
*.md

# Coverage and test reports.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov
*-testresults.xml

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.ipynb_checkpoints
